#pragma code_page(65001)
// res/lang/hy.rc -- Armenian (Armenian script), the strings of the interface for `[general] language = "hy"`.
//
// Stage E108, group A: the two string tables of this language -- the dialog block and the menu
// block -- in the order of en.rc. An adaptation, not a letter-for-letter translation (owner's word
// 198.14); the glossary of the language is l10n/glossary/hy.tsv in the control contour. Keys stay
// in Latin letters as the hotkey field prints them (RULES 4); the quotation marks are « » and the
// punctuation is Armenian (RULES 3): the full stop «։» (U+0589), the Armenian comma «՝» (U+055D) inside
// a sentence; a label and its value are joined by the plain colon «:» (the guard reads «label: {n}»,
// RULES 7); the question mark «՞» stands over the stressed vowel of the
// question word. The address of the reader is the polite plural («դուք», imperative in -եք), as
// Windows speaks Armenian; the Armenian verb has no gender, so the author's «I» needs no choice
// (RULES 14). The orthography is the reformed one, as in Armenia.
//
// ⚠ In an .rc string a backslash is an escape -- one backslash is written as two -- and a double
// quote inside a string is written as two double quotes. The code page line above is this
// file's own: without it rc.exe reads the file in the ANSI code page, silently.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Armenian — `[general] language = "hy"`.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
